; A value track targets NodePath("Ghost:position") — "Ghost" does not exist
; anywhere in this scene. CURRENT behavior: the render-side parser
; (animationResolver.ts) is THREE-free and doesn't verify targets exist, so
; the track parses normally into a GodotTrack; at mount, three.js's own
; PropertyBinding silently no-ops a track whose target can't be found (no
; crash, no visible effect) — see Component.degraded-path.test.tsx. NO
; linter rule currently inspects individual Animation track target NodePaths
; (only root_node/autoplay/current_animation existence are checked), so this
; fixture lints completely clean today — that absence of a diagnostic is the
; corpus-pinned CURRENT state, not an asserted correctness claim.

